From 6a2bc2d1a5a9e924bb07a5f6f88fcb10268f6338 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 02:05:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/46] DucoBoxSerial: add native hardware plugin

Adds a native C++ hardware plugin for the DucoBox ventilation controller,
kept in sync with the Domoticz-python-plugin implementation.

- Serial command polling with capability-based child device publishing;
  startup probe and runtime sensor handling (temp/RH/CO2/switch/fan/airflow).
- Zero-only temperature suppression with per-node non-zero memory,
  temperature filter capped at 60C, CO2 published as an explicit ppm
  custom sensor instead of AirQuality/VOC.
- Temperature is read from the already-fetched `network` table's own `temp`
  column whenever a node reports one there, instead of issuing a separate
  `NodeParaGet <node> 73` call every poll cycle; falls back to the
  parameter read only for nodes/firmwares where the table omits it.
- New "Flow" custom sensor (Dutch "debiet"): capacity (from nodeconfig,
  m3/h) times the node's airflow position percent / 100, published in the
  same unit as capacity.
- Writable config (thresholds, capacities, setpoints) is read at startup
  and on any topology change as before, but is now also re-read on a
  capped weekly cadence (`DUCO_CONFIG_REFRESH_SECONDS`) since it otherwise
  only changes when explicitly written and does not need polling every
  cycle.
- Publish the `network` table's own `stat`/`cntdwn`/`ovrl` columns as
  telemetry wherever they're populated (valves/CLIMA/box): `stat` as a
  Selector Switch (Auto/Manual 1/2/3) rather than a plain text sensor so it
  doesn't duplicate information across two device widgets; `cntdwn` as a
  countdown-in-seconds custom sensor; `ovrl` as an Override Active switch
  (on when != 255). No extra command needed since this is the same
  `network` read already done every poll cycle.
- Detect and auto-remediate a hardware fault where an RH sensor's raw
  reading (`nodeparaget <node> 75`) latches onto a high value and stops
  updating, which then drives the fan hard trying to satisfy a phantom
  humidity level. Detection requires the *raw* centi-percent value (not
  the rounded percent) to stay bit-identical for at least 20 minutes at
  >=80%, since real readings -- even during a plateaued real shower --
  still show a few raw units of ADC jitter poll to poll; this was
  validated against 6 months of real device history, where looser
  heuristics (rounded-percent flat, or fan-pinned-near-max) both fired
  constantly on ordinary shower use. Remediation issues `NodeSetOverrule`
  directly against the affected valve (mirroring the known physical fix:
  press button 1 on the associated control unit and let it time out back
  to Auto), holds it briefly, then explicitly releases it back to Auto
  itself rather than trusting the box's own countdown; a cooldown prevents
  retriggering if a given attempt doesn't clear it.
- Send `CoreLogLevel 0x10` on connect to silence asynchronous log frames
  at the source (confirmed from the firmware `help` output) instead of
  relying on a broad completion-marker workaround; `incorrect cmd arguments`
  treated as a terminal reply token in both the completion loop and the
  node-parameter value guard.
- Writable setpoints, thresholds and fan levels: every writable nodeconfig
  parameter is published data-driven from `nodeconfigget` (range straight
  from the CLI `[min:step:max]`) as Setpoint or Off/On selector devices;
  box vent-ctrl balance and temperature thresholds from `ventctrlparaget`.
  WriteToHardware decodes the Domoticz device write, routes it back to
  NodeConfigSet/VentCtrlParaSet via a marker-based device-id scheme
  (id1=0xDC,id2=group,id3=node,id4=index), issues NodeSaveData, then
  re-reads so Domoticz reflects the value the box actually stored (it may
  clamp). A command mutex guards the one serial port between the Domoticz
  worker thread (writes) and the poll thread (reads).
- Deterministic FNV-1a device-id hashing (StableKey16ForCapability),
  replacing std::hash which is implementation-defined across toolchains.
- Poll `FanPerformGet` each cycle and publish instantaneous power draw as
  a box-level Usage/Wattage device.

Verified to compile with g++ 14.2 / C++17 against the Domoticz 2026.2
headers (syntax-only) on rogue.local.

Signed-off-by: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>

Assisted-by: GPT-5.3-Codex
